<!--
  "Next in the series" card — renders below a show view when the
  current page is part of a series AND a later-positioned item exists
  in the same series. Functionally the series-ordered counterpart of
  `_next_item.html.erb` (which uses chronological order).

  Reuses the `_post_list` partial for the card body so the cover /
  meta / description follow the same per-card toggles as the rest of
  the posts collection.

  Required: the page must have BOTH `series:` and `series_position:`
  in frontmatter and there must be a next page in the series.
  `site.next_in_series` returns nil in every other case, and this
  partial renders nothing.

  Used by:  post.html.erb (in place of `_next_item` when the post is
             in a series with a later position to advance to)
-->
<% next_post = site.next_in_series(page) %>
<% if next_post %>
<section class="next-item next-item--series" aria-labelledby="next-in-series-heading">
  <h2 id="next-in-series-heading" class="next-item__heading">Next in the series</h2>
  <%== render 'partials/post_list', posts: [next_post] %>
</section>
<% end %>
